# The public npm registry, stated explicitly.
#
# GoDaddy runs `npm install --production` on its own build machine, with
# whatever npm config that machine happens to carry. If a host-level or
# account-level .npmrc points at a mirror or a private proxy, the install
# either fails or resolves packages this project has never seen. A
# project-level .npmrc wins over both, so pinning the registry here makes the
# install identical on GoDaddy, on Vercel and on a laptop.
#
# Keep this file free of auth tokens. Every dependency here is public; an
# `//registry.../:_authToken=` line in a committed .npmrc is a leaked
# credential, and nothing in this project needs one.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
